Take a reference on the context for the lifetime of a stream

pa_stream_new_with_proplist stores the context pointer:

    s->c = c;

without taking a reference, and pa_stream_unref then dereferences it during
teardown:

    s->ref_cnt--;
    if (s->ref_cnt == 0) {
        g_hash_table_remove(s->c->streams_ht, GINT_TO_POINTER(s->idx));

while pa_context_unref frees the context and destroys that table:

    c->ref_cnt--;
    if (c->ref_cnt == 0) {
        g_hash_table_unref(c->streams_ht);
        free(c->name);
        free(c);
    }

A client that drops the context before the stream therefore leaves
pa_stream_unref reading freed memory. GLib's hash lookup computes the bucket
as a modulo of the table size; read from freed memory that size is zero, and
on armhf an integer division by zero calls __aeabi_uidiv0, which raises
SIGFPE.

Observed on Volumio 4 armhf with Spotify Soloist: the daemon completes its own
shutdown, logging "shutting down", "api: websocket server stopped" and
"stopped", and only then dies. systemd records:

    soloist.service: Main process exited, code=killed, status=8/FPE
    soloist.service: Failed with result 'signal'

Under gdb the faulting thread traps in libc raise(), called from
libpulse.so.0 at file offset 0x441fa. Disassembly of that offset is the
libgcc division-by-zero landing pad:

    441f0: push {r1, lr}
    441f2: mov.w r0, #8          @ SIGFPE
    441f6: blx   raise
    441fa: pop  {r1, pc}

and the return addresses left on the stack resolve to pa_stream_unref at
0xb604, which calls the GLib hash routine at 0xdcf4, which reaches the 32-bit
unsigned division helper at 0x43adc.

Reproduces only when a stream was opened, which is why runs that never logged
in or never played exited cleanly.

s->c is dereferenced in seventeen places across apulse-stream.c, so the
context outliving its streams is a requirement of the whole file. Taking a
reference at construction and releasing it after the stream removes itself
from the table makes that ownership explicit.

--- a/src/apulse-stream.c
+++ b/src/apulse-stream.c
@@ -909,6 +909,11 @@ pa_stream_new_with_proplist(pa_context *c, const char *name,
     s->state = PA_STREAM_UNCONNECTED;
     s->ss = *ss;
 
+    // The stream dereferences s->c throughout its lifetime, including in
+    // pa_stream_unref after the client may already have dropped its own
+    // reference. Own the context rather than borrowing it.
+    pa_context_ref(c);
+
     s->idx = c->next_stream_idx++;
     g_hash_table_insert(c->streams_ht, GINT_TO_POINTER(s->idx), s);
 
@@ -1045,12 +1050,19 @@ pa_stream_unref(pa_stream *s)
 
     s->ref_cnt--;
     if (s->ref_cnt == 0) {
+        pa_context *c = s->c;
+
         g_hash_table_remove(s->c->streams_ht, GINT_TO_POINTER(s->idx));
         ringbuffer_free(s->rb);
         free(s->peek_buffer);
         free(s->write_buffer);
         free(s->name);
         free(s);
+
+        // Released only after the stream has removed itself from the table, so
+        // the table is still alive above even when this drops the last
+        // reference and frees the context.
+        pa_context_unref(c);
     }
 }
 
